; The slot a guarded case leaves in the table is never loaded, but when inlining
; has replicated a dispatch, each copy guards a different case, so a slot that
; differs between copies leaves tables that are alike everywhere except in the
; byte nothing reads -- and therefore cannot be merged. Where the case's own
; value can be recovered, it goes in the slot and the copies stay identical.

